From: meta-st-odyssey <build@local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32mp157c-odyssey: Ethernet fixes

- PHY reset at MAC level (snps,reset-gpio, 50 ms settle): mainline's per-PHY
  300 us is too short for the KSZ9031RN, so MDIO never answers ("MDIO device
  at address 7 is missing").
- Drop assigned-clocks on ethernet0: ETHCK_K has a single hardcoded parent on
  this kernel, the reparent can never succeed and is logged every boot.
- phy-mode "rgmii" as in Seeed's factory devicetree; "rgmii-id" double
  compensates the RGMII delays and leaves gigabit marginal.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [out-of-tree board]

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp157c-odyssey.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp157c-odyssey.dts
@@ -34,23 +34,22 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&ethernet0_rgmii_pins_a>;
 	pinctrl-1 = <&ethernet0_rgmii_sleep_pins_a>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
-	phy-mode = "rgmii-id";
+	phy-mode = "rgmii";
 	max-speed = <1000>;
 	phy-handle = <&phy0>;
-	assigned-clocks = <&rcc ETHCK_K>, <&rcc PLL4_P>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&rcc PLL4_P>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <125000000>; /* Clock PLL4 to 750Mhz in ATF/U-Boot */
 	st,eth-clk-sel;
 
-	mdio {
+	snps,reset-gpio = <&gpiog 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	snps,reset-active-low;
+	snps,reset-delays-us = <0 30000 50000>;
+
+	mdio0 {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
 		compatible = "snps,dwmac-mdio";
+
 		phy0: ethernet-phy@7 { /* KSZ9031RN */
 			reg = <7>;
-			reset-gpios = <&gpiog 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* ETH_RST# */
-			reset-assert-us = <10000>;
-			reset-deassert-us = <300>;
 		};
 	};
 };
